meta {
  name: signout-all
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/auth/signout/all
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Sign Out From All Devices

  Signs out the user from **all devices** by clearing all refresh tokens in their token array. This is different from `/auth/signout` which only clears the current session.

  ## Authentication

  Requires valid `zayneAccessToken` and `zayneRefreshToken` cookies.

  ## Success Response (200 OK)

  ```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "Signed out from all devices successfully",
    "data": null
  }
  ```

  **Note**:
  - Clears `zayneAccessToken` cookie
  - Clears `zayneRefreshToken` cookie
  - Invalidates all refresh tokens in user's token array (completely signs out all sessions)
  - User must sign in again on all devices

  ## Error Response (401 Unauthorized)

  If no valid session exists:

  ```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "Unauthorized"
  }
  ```

  ## Error Response (401 Unauthorized - Session Expired)

  If both tokens are expired:

  ```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "Session expired"
  }
  ```

  ## Difference from /auth/signout

  - **`/auth/signout`**: Signs out current device only (removes current token from array)
  - **`/auth/signout/all`**: Signs out all devices (clears entire token array)
}
